{"id":"n-20261023-uzyuqz","category":"tech","display_title":"Tesla And SpaceX Merger","display_title_he":"מיזוג בין טסלה וספייס אקס","short_summary":"Elon Musk has revealed that special committees are exploring a potential mega-merger between Tesla and SpaceX, which could create a multi-trillion-dollar corporate giant.","english_level":"C1","words":451,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"BBC News","domain":"bbc.co.uk","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr93z1e87e0do","title":"Why is Elon Musk plotting a mega-merger of SpaceX and Tesla?","published_at":"2026-10-21T23:04:03.000Z"},{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/21/elon-musk-tesla-spacex","title":"Tesla beats earnings projections after Musk floats SpaceX merger plan","published_at":"2026-10-21T23:03:16.000Z"},{"name":"NPR","domain":"npr.org","url":"https://www.npr.org/2026/10/22/nx-s1-6010634/elon-musk-says-space-x-and-tesla-are-considering-a-merger","title":"Elon Musk says Space X and Tesla are considering a merger","published_at":"2026-10-22T08:56:38.000Z"},{"name":"CNBC","domain":"cnbc.com","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/22/elon-musk-midterm-election-spacex-tesla.html","title":"SpaceX and Tesla have high election stakes as Elon Musk pours $366 million into campaigns","published_at":"2026-10-22T21:58:42.000Z"},{"name":"The Verge","domain":"theverge.com","url":"https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1016879/spacex-tesla-cursed-katamari","title":"Sure, let’s smoosh SpaceX and Tesla together, who cares","published_at":"2026-10-22T19:45:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-21T23:03:16.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-23T06:24:11.758Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Elon Musk is currently considering a monumental business move that could bring together two of his most prominent technology empires, Tesla and SpaceX. During recent earnings calls, the chief executive confirmed that special committees have been established to assess a potential merger between the car manufacturer and the aerospace company. When asked if the combination would be a good idea, Musk answered clearly in the affirmative, noting that he sees a lot to be gained, though he stressed that nothing has been agreed and calling it a certainty would be overstating things. Describing the process on Wednesday, Musk quipped that he felt like he was tap-dancing through a minefield.","With Tesla valued at approximately $1.5 trillion and SpaceX valued at roughly $2 trillion, a successful union would create the largest corporate merger in history. According to financial experts, the two businesses share significant technological overlap, ranging from artificial intelligence and advanced robotics to solar panels, batteries, data centres, and Starlink satellite internet systems. Proponents of the deal argue that uniting these capabilities under one roof could streamline research and eliminate internal licensing costs, allowing Tesla to utilize intellectual property and engineering design without writing checks between subsidiaries, thereby accelerating innovations like autonomous driving, humanoid Optimus robots, and Musk's ultimate vision of building a self-sustaining city on Mars.","Despite the potential benefits, the path to a combined company faces several formidable hurdles. Most notably, any transaction would require the backing of at least half of Tesla's voting shareholders, a threshold Musk himself described as quite a high hurdle, particularly since he cannot participate in shareholder discussions as boss of both firms. While analysts suggest that investors may ultimately support the move due to the complementary nature of the technologies, some institutional investors might hesitate to forfeit control, dilute Tesla's core automotive focus with rockets, or see their stakes altered in a business where vehicles may become an afterthought compared to AI infrastructure. Furthermore, regulatory scrutiny could intensify, given SpaceX's role as a major U.S. defense contractor and Tesla's manufacturing footprint in China, creating potential friction with Beijing or Washington.","Meanwhile, Tesla recently reported a solid third-quarter revenue of $28.05 billion, slightly outperforming Wall Street expectations of $27.9 billion, despite facing fierce competition from cheaper electric vehicle makers in China like BYD, which previously overtook Tesla as the world's biggest EV maker. The company also recently showcased a futuristic electric Roadster equipped with rocket-thruster technology developed by SpaceX, capable of performing rolls and gymnastics, which served as a symbolic preview of what a combined enterprise might achieve. As discussions continue, market watchers remain focused on whether shareholders, regulatory bodies, and complex global markets will ultimately clear the way for Musk's most ambitious corporate consolidation to date."],"facts":[{"fact":"Elon Musk is considering a merger between Tesla and SpaceX, forming special committees to explore the potential deal.","sources":[1,2,3]},{"fact":"Tesla is valued at roughly $1.5 trillion and SpaceX at $2 trillion, making the potential combination the largest merger ever.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Any merger would require the approval of at least 50% of Tesla shareholders.","sources":[1,2,3]},{"fact":"Tesla reported third-quarter revenue of $28.05 billion, beating Wall Street projections of $27.9 billion.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Musk recently unveiled the Tesla Roadster, an electric car featuring SpaceX rocket thrusters.","sources":[1,2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Elon Musk","lemma":"Elon Musk","pos":"PROPN","he":"אלון מאסק","name":"true"},{"text":"currently","lemma":"currently","pos":"ADV","he":"כעת","name":false},{"text":"considering","lemma":"consider","pos":"VERB","he":"שוקל","name":false},{"text":"monumental","lemma":"monumental"